  "chapter": {
    "number": 15,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(16) A writing of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Keep me, O Lord; for I have hoped in you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I said to the Lord, You are my Lord; for you have no need of my",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 26
          },
          {
            "text": "goodness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "On behalf of the saints that are in his land, he has magnified all his pleasure in them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Their weaknesses have been multiplied; afterward they hasted. I will by no means assemble their bloody meetings, neither will I make mention of their names with my lips.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord is the portion of my inheritance and of my cup: you are he that restores my inheritance to me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The lines have fallen to me in the best places, yes, I have a most excellent heritage.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will bless the Lord who has instructed me; my reins too have chastened me even",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 27
          },
          {
            "text": "till night.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I foresaw the Lord always before my face; for he is on my right hand, that I should not be moved.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore my heart rejoiced and my tongue exulted; moreover also my flesh shall rest in hope:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "because you will not leave my soul in hell, neither will you suffer your Holy One to see corruption.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have made known to me the ways of life; you will fill me with joy with your countenance: at your right hand there are delights for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 26,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. good deeds, or things.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 15,
          "verse": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 27,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Possibly, during the night. q. d. as long as night lasted.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 15,
          "verse": 7
        }
      }
    ]
  },
